NAME
       strings - print the readable text found inside a file

SYNOPSIS
       strings [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       strings looks through a file, usually a program or another binary file,
       and prints every run of at least four printable characters it finds,
       one per line. It is a quick way to see messages, file paths or version
       numbers built into a program without running it.

EXAMPLES
       Look for configuration paths inside the sshd program:

           strings /usr/sbin/sshd | grep /etc/

SEE ALSO
       file(1), xxd(1), od(1)
